/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_Math_Complex Complex
 * @ingroup Foundation_Math
 *
 * @brief Cartesian complex numbers for signed arithmetic types.
 *
 * `Complex<T>` stores public `real` and `imag` parts and provides the usual
 * arithmetic, comparison, conjugation, and squared-magnitude operations.
 * The module is enabled by `FOUNDATION_MATH_COMPLEX` and does not depend on
 * the full C++ standard library or on floating-point support, so integer
 * specializations remain usable on targets without an FPU.
 * CPSTL traits reject unsigned types, bool and non-arithmetic types.
 * Signed integer types, float, double and long double use the same class.
 * Values are trivially copyable and store two T components.
 *
 * Arithmetic follows native C++ rules for T, including integral promotions;
 * results are explicitly converted back to T. There is no conversion to float,
 * automatic saturation, fixed-point format or overflow detection. Integer
 * division truncates toward zero. All intermediate expressions and stored
 * results must be representable. A divisor's squared magnitude must be nonzero
 * and representable in its expression type (the promoted type for small integers).
 * Negating the minimum signed integer also requires caller care.
 * These scalar operations do not define fixed-point FFT scaling or twiddle formats.
 *
 * @code
 * Foundation::Math::Complex<float> z(3.0f, 4.0f);
 * Foundation::Math::Complex<float> product = z * z.Conjugate();
 * // product.real == 25.0f, product.imag == 0.0f
 * @endcode
 */
